            <ArticleTitle>The role of articular cartilage in patellofemoral pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes a conservative program of treatment for patellofemoral pain of chondromalacic origin. It has become obvious that patellofemoral pain syndromes are derived from cartilage degradation and from soft-tissue changes, including tendinitis and neuromatous degeneration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
